"""Concatenate two environment paths avoiding repeats.

`old` is the environment string before the base class initialize function is
called and `new` is the string after the call. The new string will be a fixed
string if it is not obtained from the current enviroment, or the same as the
old string if obtained from the same enviroment. The aim is not to append the
new string if it is already contained in the old string so as to limit the
growth of the environment string.
"""
def _merge(old: str, new: str) -> str {
    if new in old {
        return old;
    }
    if not old {
        return new;
    }
    return ';'.join([old, new]);
}

